dfn3_rs implements DeepFilterNet3 inference.

DSP, streaming conventions, and model parameters are derived from DeepFilterNet
by Hendrik Schroeter and contributors:
https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet
Upstream revision: 7b14b895fe7fc42cab72b4a4c1e49c982bd6404b
Upstream model archive: models/DeepFilterNet3_onnx.tar.gz

weights/dfn3.bin contains reordered and padded matrices and folded convolution
weights. Encoder matrices are FP32; decoder matrices are IEEE binary16. Biases
and convolution taps remain FP32. SHA256:
6f6148765e2ded639370d7ee6b4e6a39989c7900986461ac0cd826459904cd4e

DeepFilterNet code and model weights are MIT OR Apache-2.0. Original license
texts are included in LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE. This is an independent
implementation, not an official DeepFilterNet release.

Changes in this copy (vendored into zali-messenger core/vendor/dfn3_rs from crates.io
dfn3_rs 0.1.2, upstream commit d65d0d12227dc8076ee9ac33b4ff52b1c2e7f1bb, 2026-11-25):

- src/simd.rs: NEON kernels for aarch64 (packed GEMM/GEMV with FP16 weights converted by
  FCVTL/FCVTL2, GRU gates and tanh), mirroring the x86 AVX2 ones. Upstream runs the scalar
  path on aarch64: ~2.1 ms per 10 ms frame on Apple M-series, 64 us with these kernels.
  Output matches upstream's scalar path and the reference DeepFilterNet implementation
  (deep_filter / deep-filter-rt) within -84 dB.
- src/weights.rs: `expand` is unused on aarch64 (allow(dead_code)); src/simd.rs: the `avx2`
  flag is unused off x86_64 (allow(dead_code)).
- Cargo.toml rewritten (publish = false); Cargo.lock, README badges and CI files dropped.
  weights/dfn3.bin is unchanged (SHA256 above).
